{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the harsh sunlight assaulting his eyes. He sat up in bed, a strange, almost clinical awareness settling over him. The room was…perfect. Too perfect. The floral wallpaper was a shade of pastel that felt aggressively cheerful, the neatly arranged books on the shelf seemed staged, and the sunlight streamed in at an impossibly golden angle. He reached for his glasses, and as his fingers brushed the plastic frame, a notification popped up in his vision: \"Quest Log Updated: Acquire Glasses (Easy)\".  A wave of nausea washed over him.  He looked at his hands, noticing the unnaturally smooth skin, the perfectly manicured nails.  A digital HUD overlaid his vision, displaying health, stamina, and a bizarre inventory listing \"Rusty Sword,\" \"Healing Potion (x3),\" and \"Basic Leather Armor.\"  This wasn't his bedroom. This wasn't reality. He was *in* a video game.\n\n***\n\nPanic clawed at his throat. He stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling strangely…solid, almost *too* solid.  A chime echoed in his ears, followed by a quest objective: \"Speak with Old Man Hemlock in Oakhaven Village.\"  Oakhaven Village?  The HUD displayed a map, a vibrant, almost cartoonish rendering of a landscape he'd never seen. He glanced at his reflection in a nearby mirror.  His hair was perfectly styled, his clothes were…medieval?  He was wearing a tunic and trousers of a drab, unremarkable brown.  This was insane.  He had to figure out how this happened, how to escape, but for now, he had a quest.  He took a deep breath, the air smelling of pine and something vaguely…artificial.  \"Alright,\" he muttered, \"Old Man Hemlock, here I come.\"\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.10078337788581848}